    "id": "privacy-policy",
    "layout": "default",
    "showInNav": false,
    "translations": {
      "en": {
        "slug": "privacy-policy",
        "title": "Privacy Policy",
        "description": "Privacy Policy",
        "content": [
          "#  Privacy Policy\n\n# Privacy Policy\n\nThis privacy policy (\"Policy\") explains how IDURAR collects, uses, and discloses personal information when you (\"User\") access or use the IDURAR no-code SaaS platform (\"Platform\"). By using the Platform, you agree to the terms of this Policy.\n\n## 1. Information Collection\n\n1.1 Personal Information: The Company may collect personal information such as name, email address, and contact details voluntarily provided by Users when registering an account or using certain features of the Platform.\n\n1.2 Usage Data: The Company may collect usage data, including but not limited to IP addresses, device information, browser type, and operating system, to improve the functionality and performance of the Platform.\n\n1.3 Cookies: The Platform may use cookies or similar technologies to enhance User experience and provide personalized content. Users can manage cookie preferences through their browser settings.\n\n## 2. Information Use\n\n2.1 Service Delivery: The Company may use personal information to provide the requested services, authenticate Users, and communicate with them regarding their accounts, transactions, or support requests.\n\n2.2 Platform Improvement: The Company may analyze usage patterns and feedback to improve the features, functionality, and security of the Platform.\n\n2.3 Marketing Communications: With User consent, the Company may send promotional or marketing communications regarding the Platform. Users have the option to opt out of receiving such communications at any time.\n\n2.4 Legal Compliance: The Company may use and disclose personal information as required by law, regulations, or court orders, or to protect its rights, property, or safety, or the rights, property, or safety of Users or others.\n\n## 3. Information Sharing\n\nThe Company may share personal information with:\n\n- Service providers and partners who assist in the delivery of the Platform and related services, subject to confidentiality obligations.\n- Law enforcement agencies, regulatory authorities, or other third parties as required by law or to protect the Company's rights, property, or safety.\n\nThe Company does not sell or rent personal information to third parties for marketing purposes.\n\n## 4. Data Security\n\nThe Company implements reasonable security measures to protect personal information from unauthorized access, use, or disclosure. However, no data transmission over the internet or storage system is completely secure. Users should take necessary precautions to protect their account credentials and report any suspected security breaches.\n\n## 5. Third-Party Links\n\nThe Platform may contain links to third-party websites or services. This Policy does not apply to such third-party sites, and Users are encouraged to review their respective privacy policies.\n\n## 6. Children's Privacy\n\nThe Platform is not intended for use by individuals under the age of 12 . The Company does not knowingly collect personal information from children. If a parent or guardian becomes aware that their child has provided personal information, they should contact the Company to request deletion of that information.\n\n## 7. Changes to this Policy\n\nThe Company reserves the right to update or modify this Policy at any time. Users will be notified of any material changes through the Platform or via email. Continued use of the Platform after the effective date of the revised Policy constitutes acceptance of the updated terms.\n\n## 8. Contact Us\n\nIf you have any questions or concerns about this Privacy Policy, please contact us at support@idurarapp.com\n\n##  Get Early Access Now"
        ]
      }
    }
